  - In `client/src/pages/Timeline.tsx`, individual point logs are positioned and rendered using a combination of time-to-pixel conversion and a collision-handling grouping logic.

### 1. Vertical Position Calculation
The vertical position is determined by converting the log's `createdAt` time into minutes from midnight and then into pixels based on a constant hour height.

- **Constants (Lines 40-42):**
  ```tsx
  const HOUR_HEIGHT = 80;
  const TOTAL_HEIGHT = HOUR_HEIGHT * 24;
  const LOG_ENTRY_HEIGHT = 32;
  ```
- **Time to Pixel Functions (Lines 189-221):**
  ```tsx
  function minutesFromMidnight(date: Date): number {
    return date.getHours() * 60 + date.getMinutes();
  }
  function minutesToTopPx(minutes: number): number {
    return (minutes / (24 * 60)) * TOTAL_HEIGHT;
  }
  ```

### 2. Collision and Clustering Handling
To prevent overlapping, logs that occur at the same or near-same time are grouped together into "columns" within the same vertical slot. This is handled by `logLayoutMap` (Lines 500-530):

```tsx
const logLayoutMap = useMemo(() => {
  const map = new Map<number, { top: number; col: number; totalCols: number }>();
  const sorted = [...dayLogs].sort((a: any, b: any) =>
    new Date(a.createdAt).getTime() - new Date(b.createdAt).getTime()
  );
  const groups: any[][] = [];
  for (const log of sorted) {
    const created = new Date(log.createdAt);
    const min = minutesFromMidnight(created);
    const top = minutesToTopPx(min) - LOG_ENTRY_HEIGHT / 2;
    let placed = false;
    for (const group of groups) {
      const groupTop = minutesToTopPx(minutesFromMidnight(new Date(group[0].createdAt))) - LOG_ENTRY_HEIGHT / 2;
      // Collision threshold: 36 pixels (LOG_ENTRY_HEIGHT + 4)
      if (Math.abs(top - groupTop) < LOG_ENTRY_HEIGHT + 4) {
        group.push(log);
        placed = true;
        break;
      }
    }
    if (!placed) groups.push([log]);
  }
  for (const group of groups) {
    const firstCreated = new Date(group[0].createdAt);
    const groupTop = minutesToTopPx(minutesFromMidnight(firstCreated)) - LOG_ENTRY_HEIGHT / 2;
    const totalCols = group.length;
    group.forEach((log: any, idx: number) => {
      map.set(log.id, { top: groupTop, col: idx, totalCols });
    });
  }
  return map;
}, [dayLogs]);
```

### 3. Rendering Logic
The rendering uses the calculated layout to position logs side-by-side when they cluster (Lines 1252-1282):

```tsx
